//! rdtsc patch sites for the pinned FairPlay images.
//!
//! GENERATED by `/opt/data/perun-workspace/rdtsc_patches.py`; do not hand-edit.
//! Each entry is `(offset from __TEXT,__text, type)` where type selects the
//! idiom: 0 = A (9 bytes), 1 = B (12), 2 = C (10). Applying a table produces
//! byte-for-byte the same result as the linear scan it replaces, which is
//! what `patch_table_matches_scan` in `macho_loader.rs` pins.
//!
//! Why this exists: the scan read all of `__TEXT,__text` through the mapping,
//! faulting every page into the process. CoreFP's is 13.66 MiB, so the scan
//! alone accounted for ~15.8 MiB of the 24.4 MiB peak. These sites cluster
//! into 988 distinct 4 KiB pages, so patching them directly dirties only
//! those pages and leaves the other ~2 450 clean ones untouched.

